# Spec — Passage Mode v1 (UI layer)

Repo: `veydria-cartography` (web app under `web/`). You implement in an isolate
d git
worktree; nothing reaches the real tree until reviewed. **Touch ONLY the files 
named
below.** The engine and the Passage state-machine seam already exist, are commi
tted, and
are fully unit-tested — **do NOT modify, redesign, or re-implement them.**

## What already exists (your fixed contract — import, do not change)

`web/src/utils/passage.ts` is the complete, pure Passage state machine. Consume
it exactly:

```ts
import {
  initPassage,        // (opts: JourneyStateOpts) => PassageState
  passageAct,         // (state, action: Action) => PassageState   // action.ki
nd: 'continue'|'rest'|'force-march'|'ration'|'turn-back'
  passageChoose,      // (state, choiceIndex: number) => PassageState
  currentNodeIndex,   // (state) => number   // route-node index of current pos
ition
  type PassageState,  // { journey, log: PassageEntry[], extraDays, pending, ou
tcome }
  type PassageEntry,  // discriminated by .kind: 'day' | 'wait' | 'choice' | 'e
nding'
  type PassageOutcome,// 'in-progress' | 'arrived' | 'aborted' | 'perished'
  type EncounterChoice,
} from '../../utils/passage'
```

Behaviour you rely on (already guaranteed + tested — do not re-derive):
- `initPassage(opts)` seeds from the SAME inputs Atlas already has (route/seaso
n/mode/party/
  supply/edgeBiomes/departureDayOfYear). `JourneyStateOpts` is exported from `j
ourney-days.ts`.
- `passageAct(state, {kind:'continue'})` advances one day and appends a `{kind:
'day'}` entry —
  UNLESS the next day carries a signature encounter, in which case it returns a
state with
  `state.pending` set and does NOT advance. When `pending` is set, the action b
ar must be
  replaced by the choice cards; call `passageChoose(state, i)` to resolve.
- The other four actions (`rest`/`force-march`/`ration`/`turn-back`) always ste
p immediately.
- Endings: when `state.outcome !== 'in-progress'`, the journey is over and the 
last log entry
  is `{kind:'ending', outcome, narrative}`. Disable all actions.
- `state.log` is the full journal, already ordered. Render it; do not recompute
anything.

`PassageEntry` shapes (render each `.kind`):
```ts
{ kind: 'day';    dayLabel: number; day: JourneyDay; supply: SupplyDay }
{ kind: 'wait';   dayLabel: number; supply: SupplyDay; narrative: string }
{ kind: 'choice'; dayLabel: number; label: string; narrative: string; risk: 'no
ne'|'minor'|'grave' }
{ kind: 'ending'; dayLabel: number; outcome; narrative: string }
```
`SupplyDay` has `rationsLeft`, `waterLeft` (floats, may be NEGATIVE = debt — re
nder the debt,
do not clamp the number to 0; styling may flag it), and optional `warning`
(`'rations-low'|'water-low'|'rations-out'|'water-out'`). `JourneyDay` has `dayN
um`, `startLabel`,
`campLabel`, `weather`, `encounters`, `notable`. Reuse the existing day-row ren
dering idiom from
`web/src/components/journey-planner/JourneyDaysTab.tsx` for visual consistency.

## What to build

### 1. `web/src/components/journey-planner/PassageMode.tsx` (NEW)
Single-column journal takeover. Props:
```ts
interface PassageModeProps {
  route: JourneyRoute
  season?: Season
  mode: RouteMode
  party: PartyConfig
  supply: SupplyConfig
  edgeBiomes?: (string | undefined)[]
  departureDayOfYear?: number
  onExit: () => void                       // back to Atlas (planner)
  onPositionChange?: (nodeIndex: number | null) => void  // for the map marker;
null on exit
}
```
- On mount: `useState(() => initPassage({route, season, mode, party, supply, ed
geBiomes, departureDayOfYear}))`.
- Render the supply ledger (rations + water remaining, as dwindling stores; sho
w negative debt
  distinctly), the journal log (`state.log`, one block per entry kind), and bel
ow it either:
  - the **action bar** (5 buttons: Continue, Rest, Force-march, Ration, Turn ba
ck) when
    `!state.pending && state.outcome === 'in-progress'`; each calls `setState(p
assageAct(state, {kind}))`.
  - the **choice cards** when `state.pending` — one card per `state.pending.cho
ices` showing
    `choice.label` + `choice.outcome.narrative` + a risk badge; click → `setSta
te(passageChoose(state, i))`.
  - the **ending panel** when `state.outcome !== 'in-progress'` — show the fina
l narrative and a
    single button → `onExit()`.
- After every state change call `onPositionChange(currentNodeIndex(state))`; ca
ll
  `onPositionChange(null)` on unmount / exit.
- Reuse existing CSS variables (`--text-accent`, `--bg-card`, etc.) and class n
aming from the
  journey-planner components. No new color literals; match the surrounding aest
hetic.

### 2. `web/src/components/journey-planner/JourneyResults.tsx` (EDIT)
Add a single **"Set out"** button to the route summary (only meaningful when a 
route exists,
which is always true where JourneyResults renders). Wire a new optional prop
`onSetOut?: () => void` and render the button near the route stats. Do not rest
ructure the file.

### 3. `web/src/components/JourneyPlanner.tsx` (EDIT)
- Add `const  = useState(false)`.
- Pass `onSetOut={() => { setPassageActive(true); onPassageActiveChange?.(true)
}}` to `JourneyResults`.
- When `passageActive && route`, render `<PassageMode .../>` as a full takeover
of the planner
  body (in place of the normal tabs/results), feeding it the local `route, seas
on, mode, party,
  supply, edgeBiomes, departureDayOfYear`. Its `onExit` does
  `setPassageActive(false); onPassageActiveChange?.(false)`. Forward `onPositio
nChange` up via a
  new prop (see App).
- Add new optional props to `JourneyPlannerProps`:
  `onPassageActiveChange?: (active: boolean) => void` and
  `onPassagePositionChange?: (nodeIndex: number | null) => void`. Forward the l
atter to PassageMode.

### 4. `web/src/App.tsx` (EDIT) — the visual flip + position marker
- Add `const  = useState(false)` and
  `const  = useState<number | null>(null)`.
- Pass `onPassageActiveChange={setPassageActive}` and
  `onPassagePositionChange={setPassageNodeIndex}` to `<JourneyPlanner/>`.
- Add the class `passage-mode` to the existing `app-main` className string **on
ly when**
  `passageActive` (it already composes `time-of-day-${...}` the same way).
- Render a **current-position marker** on the map **only when** `passageActive 
&& passageNodeIndex != null`.
  Reuse the SAME projection the route polyline already uses (see how the journe
y route is drawn in
  `web/src/components/MapViewer.tsx`); place ONE marker at the current route no
de
  (`route.nodes`). It MUST unmount cleanly when `passageActive` goes false or
  the index is null — leaving Atlas mode renders the map exactly as before (no 
residual marker,
  no residual class). This is the one net-new render-path change; keep it addit
ive and isolated.

### 5. `web/src/App.css` (EDIT)
- `.app-main.passage-mode .leaflet-container { filter: saturate(0.55) brightnes
s(0.8); }`
  (mirror the existing `.app-main.time-of-day-*` filter rules; they already tra
nsition over 0.5s).
- Optional: let chrome recede in passage mode (e.g. dim `.layer-controls`/toolb
ar opacity). Keep
  it light; do not restructure layout.
- Style classes for PassageMode (journal, ledger, action bar, choice cards, end
ing panel,
  negative-debt indicator). Match existing journey-planner styling.

### 6. `web/e2e/smoke.spec.ts` (EDIT)
Add ONE test: compute a route (reuse the existing `computeRoute(page)` helper),
click **Set out**,
then click **Continue** repeatedly (a bounded loop, e.g. ≤40 clicks) until an e
nding panel appears,
and assert the ending panel + its exit button are visible, and that clicking ex
it returns to the
planner (`.journey-route` visible again). If you add any one-time intro localSt
orage key, gate it
in the existing `beforeEach` `addInitScript` block alongside `veydria.welcome.s
een.v1`.

## Hard constraints
- **Do NOT touch** `web/src/utils/passage.ts`, `journey-days.ts`, `journey-supp
ly.ts`,
  `encounters.ts`, or any sim file. The seam is frozen.
- Reroute is intentionally OUT of v1 — only the 5 actions above.
- All NEW player-facing prose must be em-dash-free (VOICE-SPEC Option B): no `—
` characters in
  any string literal you add. `grep -n "—"` over your new strings must be empty
. (Code comments
  are exempt.)
- TypeScript: the project's TS lib target predates `Array.prototype.at` — use i
ndex access
  (`arr`), not `.at(-1)`.
- Preserve surrounding code style; surgical edits only; no drive-by refactors.

## Acceptance criteria (all must hold)
1. From a computed route, **Set out** enters Passage mode (journal + ledger + a
ction bar visible).
2. **Continue** advances one day and appends a day block; the supply ledger dec
reases.
3. A signature-encounter day shows choice cards instead of the action bar; pick
ing a choice
   resolves it and continues the journal.
4. Reaching the destination shows the **arrived** ending; turn-back shows **abo
rted**; supply
   debt past the floor shows **perished**. Each shows its closing narrative + a
n exit button.
5. The map **dims** and shows a **current-position marker** in Passage mode; **
exiting returns
   Atlas mode unchanged** (no residual marker, no residual `passage-mode` class
).
6. `npm run test` (all existing + the seam's passage tests) stays green; `npx t
sc -b` is clean;
   `npm run test:e2e` passes including the new walk.

## Commands (run from `web/`)
- Unit: `npm run test`
- Typecheck: `npx tsc -b`
- E2E: `npm run test:e2e` (dev server auto-starts on port 5180 `--strictPort`)

## Clarifications (resolved from spec review — follow these)

These tighten the contract; they do not add scope.

- **Marker MUST reproject on zoom/resize.** This repo previously shipped a bug 
where overlays
  did not reproject on zoom (hex + constellation misposition, since fixed). The
current-position
  marker must ride the SAME overlay/redraw path the journey route polyline uses
in
  `MapViewer.tsx`, so it tracks the map on zoom and resize. Do not place a mark
er that projects
  once and goes stale. This is the single highest-risk item — verify it visuall
y.
- **Guard the marker render.** Only render when `passageActive && passageNodeIn
dex != null &&
  route.nodes` exists. `currentNodeIndex` always returns an in-range index
  (0..nodes.length-1), but keep the guard defensive.
- **Functional setState (rapid-click safety).** Use `setState(s => passageAct(s
, {kind}))` and
  `setState(s => passageChoose(s, i))`, NOT `setState(passageAct(state, ...))`.
The seam already
  no-ops invalid transitions (acting while finished or pending), so the only ri
sk is a lost
  update from stale closure — functional updates remove it.
- **Inputs are snapshotted at mount.** PassageMode is a full takeover: while it
is mounted the
  planner controls are not reachable, so route/party/supply cannot change mid-p
assage. Seed once
  via `useState(() => initPassage(...))` and do NOT reset on prop change.
- **`pending` vs logged `choice` entries are different things.** Render the cho
ice CARDS from
  `state.pending.choices` (the current, undecided encounter). Render `{kind:'ch
oice'}` entries in
  `state.log` as the historical record of PAST decisions. They never double-ren
der the same choice.
- **Three render branches, mutually exclusive, in this order:** ending panel (`
outcome !==
  'in-progress'`) → choice cards (`state.pending`) → action bar. Evaluate endin
g first so a step
  that both advances and ends never shows the action bar beside an ending.
- **Position callback lifecycle.** Fire `onPositionChange(currentNodeIndex(stat
e))` on mount AND
  after every state change. Fire `onPositionChange(null)` from a `useEffect` cl
eanup (so it covers
  both the ending-exit button and `passageActive` going false). It must be idem
potent.
- **Ledger:** pin it at the top of the panel above the scrolling journal. Forma
t rations/water to
  one decimal (match the supply rendering in `JourneyDaysTab.tsx`). Negative va
lues render with a
  distinct class (e.g. `.passage-debt`) and a short "debt" affordance; do not c
lamp to 0.
- **Do not import `JourneyDaysTab`.** Write PassageMode's own markup; you may r
euse its CSS class
  names / the global CSS variables (defined in `App.css`/`index.css`, no new fi
le needed).
- **CSS precedence:** the `.app-main.passage-mode .leaflet-container` filter mu
st win over the
  `time-of-day-*` filter when both classes are present (passage dim takes prece
dence regardless of
  time of day). Define it after the time-of-day rules / give it sufficient spec
ificity.
- **Imports:** `import type { JourneyStateOpts } from '../../utils/journey-days
'`.
- **Light focus handling:** on entering Passage, move focus to the journal pane
l heading; nothing
  more elaborate is required for v1.
- **No first-run intro overlay in v1** (so no new localStorage gating is needed
).

## Additional acceptance criteria (from review)
7. All five actions (Continue, Rest, Force-march, Ration, Turn back) are visibl
e and functional;
   each produces its journal entry / supply effect. Rest burns water but not ra
tions; turn-back ends `aborted`.
8. E2E: the Continue-walk must click the first choice card whenever choice card
s appear, advance
   to an ending within the bounded loop, and **fail** (not silently pass) if no
ending is reached.
   After clicking exit, assert the planner (`.journey-route`) is visible again 
AND the
   passage-position marker is gone (assert its selector count is 0).
