5314f, see\n   419\t     veydria-schematic.svg #ocean) so the SVG edge no longe
r reads as a seam\n   420\t     against a flatter backdrop. Stays in the deep-w
ater register so the\n   421\t     time-of-day filters below keep it as water, 
not black (night drops\n   422\t     brightness to 0.5). Harmonised with the Se
a-biome (#6a8ca8) hex fills. */\n   423\t  background: linear-gradient(180deg, 
#27567e 0%, #1d4368 55%, #15314f 100%) !important;\n   424\t  font-family: var(
--font-body) !important;\n   425\t  transition: filter 0.5s ease;\n   426\t}\n 
 427\t\n   428\t/* Living-water shimmer — a faint, slow diagonal sheen drifting
over the sea.\n   429\t   mix-blend-mode: soft-light makes it read on the dark 
ocean and wash out over\n   430\t   the bright landmass, so it animates the wat
er without muddying the continent.\n   431\t   Scoped to .leaflet-container (th
e map canvas) so the React side panels are\n   432\t   untouched; z-index sits 
above the schematic/terrain overlay pane (400) but\n   433\t   below markers (6
00) and controls, and pointer-events:none keeps the map fully\n   434\t   inter
active. Inherits the time-of-day filter, so it dims at dusk/night too. */\n   4
35\t.leaflet-container::after {\n   436\t  content: \'\';\n   437\t  position: 
absolute;\n   438\t  inset: 0;\n   439\t  pointer-events: none;\n   440\t  z-in
dex: 450;\n   441\t  background: repeating-linear-gradient(\n   442\t    112deg
,\n   443\t    transparent 0 22px,\n   444\t    rgba(150, 200, 235, 0.05) 22px 
24px,\n   445\t    transparent 24px 54px\n   446\t  );\n   447\t  mix-blend-mod
e: soft-light;\n   448\t  will-change: background-position;\n   449\t  animatio
n: ocean-shimmer 19s linear infinite;\n   450\t}\n   451\t\n   452\t@keyframes 
ocean-shimmer {\n   453\t  from { background-position: 0 0; }\n   454\t  to   {
background-position: 270px -96px; }\n   455\t}\n   456\t\n   457\t@media (prefe
rs-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n   458\t  .leaflet-container::after { animation: 
none; }\n   459\t}\n   460\t\n   461\t/* Feather the schematic\'s edges so its 
fixed rectangle dissolves into the\n   462\t   surrounding ocean instead of sho
wing a hard "square around Veydria". The\n   463\t   image\'s baked gradient is
in image-space and the container gradient is in\n   464\t   viewport-space, so 
they can\'t align across zoom/pan — softening the boundary\n   465\t   is the r
obust fix. The continent sits well inside the image with an ocean\n   466\t   m
argin on every side, so this only fades open water (and never the baked\n   467
\t   country labels, which are interior). Two intersecting linear masks feather
\n   468\t   all four edges; the inset is small (~3–3.5%) to stay clear of the 
landmass. */\n   469\t.leaflet-image-layer {\n   470\t  -webkit-mask-image:\n  
471\t    linear-gradient(to right, transparent 0, #000 3%, #000 97%, transparen
t 100%),\n   472\t    linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent 0, #000 3.5%, #000
96.5%, transparent 100%);\n   473\t  -webkit-mask-composite: source-in;\n   474
\t  mask-image:\n   475\t    linear-gradient(to right, transparent 0, #000 3%, 
